{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run && cat research.json | head -80 && ls logs/8248101f2e7e47ecae3104f94cd0357b/'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"run_id\": \"750100f25c9d4b398f0475642e7e72b8\",\n  \"method\": \"audit-products-v63\",\n  \"allocation\": {\n    \"seconds\": 2964.399272937,\n    \"agent_calls\": 78,\n    \"experiments\": 39\n  },\n  \"source_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source\",\n  \"draft_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft\",\n  \"state_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run/state.json\",\n  \"submission_schema\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json\",\n  \"method_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_16-25-56-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-method.md\",\n  \"directed_question\": null,\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"investigations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce1a7dcb68b449448fdee06b3eb7737e-question-0\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"question\": \"In the captured snapshot, is a leadership-transfer order (TimeoutNow) bound at the receiver to the current leader's authority, or can a delivered order that carries no term and whose claimed sender is not the current leader (and not a configuration member) drive a stable follower out of Follower and depose the serving leader?\",\n      \"hypothesis\": \"Raft.timeoutNow is the only RPC handler that changes authority without consulting any term: it does setLeader(\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\"), setState(Candidate) and candidateFromLeadershipTransfer.Store(true) and responds, ignoring RPCHeader.ID/Addr and the configuration. TimeoutNowRequest embeds only RPCHeader, so no term/freshness value exists to check, while the producer only sends it after it has caught the target up (nextIndex beyond the leader's last index) - a precondition the receiver cannot verify. The Candidate run skips pre-vote (raft.go:294-298) and voters skip the known-leader rejection for LeadershipTransfer candidates (raft.go:1645-1656), so the order withdraws both disruption guards at once.\",\n      \"discriminator\": \"In one fault-free, normally bootstrapped 3-node in-memory cluster with a stable leader at a known term, deliver a single TimeoutNow to a follower using a transport RPC header whose ID is not a configuration member (and which necessarily carries no term), then observe the target's state/term and the previous leader's state/term for a bounded interval. Control: the same non-member sender with a RequestVoteRequest that does carry a term, but an older one, must leave the target unchanged. If the TimeoutNow leaves the target in Follower at the same term and the leader in place, the hypothesis is refuted; if the target leaves Follower at a higher term while the leader steps down, the receiver-side authority gap is observed.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s_timeoutnow_handler\",\n        \"s_timeoutnow_msg\",\n        \"s_prevote_gate\",\n        \"s_vote_known_leader\",\n        \"s_sender_precondition\"\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence\": [],\n      \"limitations\": [\n        \"The probe uses the in-memory transport inside one process; the sender identity is the RPC header ID, and the network transport does not authenticate peers at the Raft layer, so the spoofed-identity route overlaps with transport-level trust. The freshness part of the question does not depend on spoofing: a replayed or delayed order from a legitimate former leader is indistinguishable because the message carries no term.\",\n        \"The probe observes disruption/authority behaviour only. It does not claim a state-machine safety violation (log matching and vote uniqueness are still enforced by the term/vote rules), and it does not establish how long the deposed leader's clients are without a leader.\",\n        \"No claim is made about clusters where no leader is currently known; the probe starts from a stable leader to make the authority transition observable.\"\n      ],\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"knowledge\": [],\n      \"open_gaps\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ce1a7dcb68b449448fdee06b3eb7737e-gap-0\",\n          \"question\": \"Does one received TimeoutNow, whose RPC header claims a sender that is not the serving leader and not a configuration member and which carries no term, actually move a stable follower out of Follower at a higher term and cause the serving leader to step down in a fault-free 3-node cluster, while a stale-term RequestVote from the same claimed sender leaves the target unchanged?\",\n          \"experiment_id\": null,\n          \"operation_id\": \"ce1a7dcb68b449448fdee06b3eb7737e\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"latest_execution\": {\n        \"id\": \"8248101f2e7e47ecae3104f94cd0357b\",\n        \"experiment_id\": \"ce1a7dcb68b449448fdee06b3eb7737e-experiment\",\n        \"status\": \"completed\",\n        \"exit_code\": 0,\n        \"record\": \"logs/8248101f2e7e47ecae3104f94cd0357b/check.json\",\n        \"observations\": \"logs/8248101f2e7e47ecae3104f94cd0357b/observations.json\"\n      },\n      \"latest_interpretation\": null,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n        \"id\": \"ce1a7dcb68b449448fdee06b3eb7737e-question-0\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce1a7dcb68b449448fdee06b3eb7737e-question-1\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"question\": \"Can a server in the captured snapshot hold a configurations.latest (and hence GetConfiguration) that is older than its own committed log, and how is that state produced?\",\n      \"hypothesis\": \"GetConfiguration returns the atomically published latest configuration (api.go:897-903), a value written only by setLatestConfiguration. In the captured package's own TestRaft_ProtocolVersion_Upgrade_2_3, an old follower was observed reporting the 2-server bootstrap configuration for at least the full 5s EnsureSamePeers window while the newly added server reported the 3-server configuration, i.e. the membership read diverged from the replicated configuration entry. A candidate production path is the rollback in appendEntries (raft.go:1526-1532, setLatestConfiguration(committed, committedIndex)) combined with the duplicate-skip loop that never re-runs processConfigurationLogEntry for an entry already present.\",\n      \"discriminator\": \"Replay the captured upgrade scenario with instrumentation that reads configurations.latest/latestIndex, the atomic latestConfiguration, the log store contents and commitIndex on every node immediately after the AddVoter future returns and then every 250ms; a persistent latest index below the appended configuration entry index (with the entry present in the log store and applied to the FSM) would confirm the divergence, while convergence within a few hundred ms on every run would show the earlier observation was lag rather than a stale read.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s_get_configuration\",\n        \"s_ensure_same_peers\"\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence\": [],\n      \"limitations\": [\n        \"Local exploration only: the captured TestRaft_ProtocolVersion_Upgrade_2_3 failed with 'peer mismatch' in 2 of 3 isolated local runs, but two instrumented re-implementations of the same scenario converged within 250ms on every run, so the mechanism is unresolved rather than established. No knowledge entry is claimed here.\",\n        \"The frozen evidence for any claim must come from the controller's own execution of a fixed harness, which has not been requested for this question.\"\n      ],\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\ncheck.json\nobservations.json\nstderr.log\nstdout.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
